  "problem": {
    "token_boundary": "With explicitly raised max_steps, 2500 pure touchpad.capabilities operations completed but exceeded the unchanged 65536-token parser limit; CLI returned nonzero and MCP could lose the response.",
    "encoding_boundary": "2200 operations fit the parser token limit but the text plus structured MCP envelope exceeded the prior fixed escaping allowance, producing Buffer needed=1263385 and terminating the stdio session.",
    "red_is_runtime_assertion_failure_not_compilation_failure": true
  },
  "decisions": [
    "Keep the original default max_steps=256 and supported explicit execution budgets. Detailed event logging does not reduce those execution limits.",
    "Use the locked parser actual token count and the existing 768KiB detail budget. Retain a strict prefix and expose events_omitted for all later omitted details.",
    "Reserve 256 parser tokens for final receipt/envelope fields. Keep cleanup attempted/failed counters outside optional details and preserve execution, cancellation and cleanup errors, including dual failure.",
    "Retry only the already computed MCP result serialization once, using Writer.needed and the existing 32MiB encoded-response ceiling. Never re-enter Runtime or replay actions."
  ],
